@page "/Blog"
@page "/Blog/{Filter}"

<PageTitle>Blog</PageTitle>

<MudStack>
	<BlogBlock Title="Website hosting on GitHub" CreationDate=DateTime.Now Filter=@Filter>
		<BlogHeader>
			<MudText>For this project, I wanted to use Blazor to create my own website with minimal hosting coosts.</MudText>
			<MudText>This solution that you see on this page is where I am currrently with MudBlazor using Blazor WASM and hosting on GitHub pages.</MudText>
		</BlogHeader>

		<BlogBody>
			<MudText>This solution that I landed on is very nice, but it does come with some pretty noticable pros and cons.</MudText>
			<ProsConsList>
				<Pros>
					<ol type="1" style="margin-left: 20px;">
						<li><MudText>Free hosting!!</MudText></li>
						<li><MudText>GitHub Action support</MudText></li>
						<li><MudText>MudBlazor UI framework</MudText></li>
					</ol>
				</Pros>
				<Cons>
					<ol type="1" style="margin-left: 20px;">
						<li><MudText>Load times - The loading animation while cute is there to hide the time it takes for Blazor to inject itself</MudText></li>
						<li><MudText>Page navigation is technically done by rerouting off of the GitHub 404 page lol</MudText></li>
						<li><MudText>Metadata on properly works on the home page</MudText></li>
					</ol>
				</Cons>
			</ProsConsList>
			<MudText>For my use case, the hard-learnings and low-cost were perfect.</MudText>
			<MudSpacer/>

			<MudCard Elevation=5>
				<MudCardHeader>
					<MudText Typo=Typo.h6>How I did this</MudText>
				</MudCardHeader>
				<MudCardContent>
					<ol type="1" style="margin-left: 20px;">
						<li>
							<MudText>
								Create a new GitHub repository following this documentation: <MudLink Href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/creating-a-github-pages-site" Target="_blank">Create a github pages site</MudLink>
							</MudText>
						</li>
						<li>
							<MudText>
								Create a new MudBlazor WASM starting template in your repo.  You can follow the directions from here:
								<MudLink Href="https://mudblazor.com/getting-started/installation#using-templates" Target="_blank">Mud Blazor Getting Started</MudLink>
								<MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning">Ensuring that you select "WebAssembly" is important here as GitHub pages cannot host a full Blazor Server application.</MudAlert>
							</MudText>
						</li>
						<li>
							<MudText>Double check and ensure you have a <code>base href="/"</code> block in your index.html.  This is very important for asset navigation in local and published environments.</MudText>
							<MudText>My source code: <MudLink Href="https://github.com/TortoiseEatToes/tortoiseeattoes.github.io/blob/main/wwwroot/index.html#L6" Target="_blank">launchSettings.json</MudLink></MudText>
						</li>
						<li>
							<MudText>
								Set your project up to auto-deploy to GitHub pages by following this documentation:
								<MudLink Href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/blazor/host-and-deploy/webassembly/github-pages?view=aspnetcore-10.0" Target="_blank">Blazor host and depoy</MudLink>
							</MudText>
						</li>
						<li>
							<MudText>Finally, modify your action to meet your needs. In my case, I also added a block to update the publish tag for fun.
								<MudLink Href="https://github.com/TortoiseEatToes/PersonalWebsite/blob/main/.github/workflows/static.yml#L52" Target="_blank">static.yml</MudLink>
							</MudText>
							<MudText>You can see my finished version of that action here: <MudLink Href="https://github.com/TortoiseEatToes/PersonalWebsite/blob/main/.github/workflows/static.yml" Target="_blank">static.yml</MudLink></MudText>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</MudCardContent>
			</MudCard>
			<MudSpacer />

			<MudCard Elevation=5>
				<MudCardHeader>
					<MudText Typo=Typo.h6>Pitfalls to watch out for:</MudText>
				</MudCardHeader>
				<MudCardContent>
					<ol type="1" style="margin-left: 20px;">
						<li>
							<MudText>Verify that your base href is correct in your GitHub action.</MudText>
							<MudText>If you want to publish your site directly onto your user GitHub path you do NOT want to override this value.  So you should ensure that this block is removed from your code</MudText>
							<code style="display: block; white-space: pre-wrap;">
								- name: Rewrite base href
								uses: SteveSandersonMS/ghaction-rewrite-base-href@5b54862a8831e012d4f1a8b2660894415fdde8ec # v1.1.0
								with:
								html_path: ${{ env.PUBLISH_DIR }}/index.html
								base_href: /{YOUR_REPO_NAME}/
							</code>
						</li>
						<li>
							<MudText>Ensure that you set the .nojekly and 404 redirect logic!</MudText>
							<MudLink Href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/blazor/host-and-deploy/webassembly/github-pages?view=aspnetcore-10.0#deployment-notes" Target="_blank">static.yml</MudLink>
						</li>
						<li>
							<MudText>In your 404.html file, make sure that this is set to <code>var segmentCount = 0;</code> if your href is "/".  If not ,it needs to be <code>var segmentCount = 1;</code></MudText>
						</li>
					</ol>
				</MudCardContent>
			</MudCard>
			<MudSpacer />

			<MudText>Lessons learned</MudText>
			<MudSpacer />

			<MudText>Handy debugging tools:</MudText>
			<ol type="1" style="margin-left: 20px;">
				<li><MudText><MudLink Href="https://discord.com/developers/embeds?url=https%253A%252F%252Ftortoiseeattoes.github.io" Target="_blank">Discord Embed Debugger</MudLink> was very helpful for iterating on my metadata tags and image links.</MudText></li>
			</ol>
		</BlogBody>
	</BlogBlock>
</MudStack>

@code {
	[Parameter]
	public string? Filter { get; set; } = "SaraTest";
}
